ID: vr-50
Title: Calm browser workspace and floating-head controls

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: One coherent, readable UI across the manager and existing face players
Dependencies: vr-45, vr-46, vr-47
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/49

Purpose:
  Put session selection, speech and deliberate customization ahead of competing
  controls. Preserve every existing model, color choice and native ownership
  boundary. Apply researched hierarchy/material/accessibility principles rather
  than copying another application's visual effects or implementation.

Tasks:
  Review the requested design discussion, its images and explicit document
  references. Inventory actual Verona surfaces and protect the live runtime.
  Implement a calmer manager, grouped browser controls and fitted native menus.
  Preserve focused controls, per-head unsent drafts and explicit stale/error
  feedback. Qualify actual interactions and representative rendered layouts.
  Update the engineering book and causal ledger; contribute grounded learnings
  back to the requested discussion after qualification.

Acceptance criteria:
  All six existing variants and all five arbitrary feature colors remain.
  Editable now and Read-only settings retain their distinct meanings.
  Pin/name stay inside default-collapsed floating menus; pin remains default-on.
  Polling does not replace focused session targets or unsent speech/color edits.
  Speech acceptance never clears another head's draft or newly typed text.
  Loading, empty, stale, pending and failed states do not masquerade as success.
  Browser/narrow/keyboard and actual native transparency/controls are checked
  with isolated fixtures and owned profiles, without driving existing heads.
  No new renderer/audio owner, device activation, external runtime assets or
  ornamental animation loop; no unmeasured performance or human-acceptance claim.

Completion evidence:
  Implemented and environment-qualified in a detached candidate at d527fe4.
  76 CPU regressions; ui-controls-04 eleven manager fixture checks and
  ui-controls-03 shared menus; ui-player-layouts-09 actual encoded wide/narrow/
  native images and MPFB alpha. ui-topmost-01 actual two-head Windows pin state.
  ui-live-01 native16/real-Edge color6checks; ui-sessions-01 all six native
  variants, actual muted speech, GUI/CLI edits and owned lifecycle/isolation.
  Representative actual images visually inspected. Earlier01..08 capture
  receipts retained/rejected; no owner visual, listening or accuracy acceptance.
  Chapter10/index/guide/causal ledger updated. Source promotion and requested
  implementation-learning contribution remain pending at this checkpoint.

Completion log:
  2026-11-21 - Began the bounded UI workstream after reading the complete
    requested discussion, illustrated reference book and additional local
    document references. Created a detached candidate worktree; no UI runtime
    edits have been promoted to the live-served checkout.
  2026-11-21 - Qualified browser/native implementation and actual six-variant
    flow with disposable state. Rejected empty/stale capture evidence rather
    than treating fixture success as a visual pass. Delivery/board follow next.
  2026-11-21 - Put standalone MPFB speech before secondary settings/previews.
    Requalified wide/narrow actual images and native pin/readiness. Separate
    narrow input and scrolled-model captures rather than require an offscreen
    mesh to appear above the fold. Prune retired unselected head drafts.
